From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: natemu <natemu@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] FEXCore: slice1 I5a SSE sites, constants and MXCSR flags

Under fexc_slice1 only (the default profile is unchanged). The allowlist,
the alignment check and the site records are in tools/fexc/shim/.

- OpcodeDispatcher.h/Vector.cpp: a vector element from or to memory (MOVHPS,
  MOVLPS, MOVHPD, MOVLPD, PINSR*, PEXTR*, EXTRACTPS m) is a plain LoadMem /
  StoreMem of the element (a recorded site, split-checked) instead of FEX's
  ld1/st1 lane ops, which the site record does not describe; MOVNTDQA and the
  16-byte MOVNT stores are plain loads and stores (ordered: allowed for MOVNT).
- VectorOps.cpp: named and indexed vector constants are built in their
  register (movz/movk into x0, fmov to the low and high halves) instead of
  loaded through the state frame (code touches no emulator data).
- MXCSR flags as x86 raises them (the resident ORs FPSR into MXCSR):
  COMISS/COMISD compare with fcmpe (invalid for a QNaN too); ROUND* with
  imm8 bit 3 clear use frintx (PE when inexact), under the instruction's
  rounding mode through an FPCR.RMode switch when imm8 bit 2 is clear;
  RCPPS/RCPSS/RSQRTPS/RSQRTSS keep FPSR across their exact division (x86
  raises no SIMD exception there). Emitter.h gains the FPSR system register.
---
diff --git a/CodeEmitter/CodeEmitter/Emitter.h b/CodeEmitter/CodeEmitter/Emitter.h
index 001adcb..6e78eec 100644
--- a/CodeEmitter/CodeEmitter/Emitter.h
